pageType: content
background:
  type: solid
  color: "$bg"
elements:
  # ---------- header ----------
  - elementId: kicker
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 38, 700, 16]
    content:
      style: "$kicker"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        THE PROBLEM — BEFORE THE TWO SOLUTIONS
  - elementId: title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 58, 760, 44]
    content:
      style: "$title"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        Same business, two kinds of wrong answers
  - elementId: title-rule
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [64, 118, 832, 1]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$line"}

  # ---------- left: failure 1 — meaning ----------
  - elementId: f1-label
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 140, 384, 12]
    content:
      fontSize: 10
      color: "$ont"
      bold: true
      letterSpacing: 1.5
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        FAILURE 1 — THE WORD MEANS DIFFERENT THINGS
  - elementId: f1-head
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 158, 384, 18]
    content:
      fontSize: 14.5
      color: "$ink"
      bold: true
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        "Customer" across the order-to-cash stack
  - elementId: f1-rows
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 184, 384, 112]
    content:
      fontSize: 11.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.35
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p><strong>Contract &amp; order system</strong> — the sold-to party who signed the deal</p>
        <p style="margin-top:8px"><strong>Billing / AR</strong> — the payer the invoice is sent to</p>
        <p style="margin-top:8px"><strong>Terminal automation</strong> — the consignee picking up at the rack</p>
        <p style="margin-top:8px"><strong>CRM</strong> — the account the sales team manages</p>
  - elementId: f1-note
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 308, 384, 44]
    content:
      fontSize: 10.5
      color: "$muted"
      italic: true
      lineHeight: 1.35
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>Same company, four systems, four lists — ask for "unbilled by customer" and each system answers about a different "customer."</p>
  - elementId: f1-verdict
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 366, 384, 16]
    content:
      fontSize: 11.5
      color: "$ink"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        <p>Root cause: <strong><span style="color:$ont">meaning</span></strong> — what a word refers to</p>

  # ---------- divider ----------
  - elementId: divider
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [480, 140, 1, 254]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$line"}

  # ---------- right: failure 2 — logic ----------
  - elementId: f2-label
    elementType: text
    bounds: [512, 140, 384, 12]
    content:
      fontSize: 10
      color: "$sl"
      bold: true
      letterSpacing: 1.5
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        FAILURE 2 — THE MATH IS DIFFERENT EVERYWHERE
  - elementId: f2-head
    elementType: text
    bounds: [512, 158, 384, 18]
    content:
      fontSize: 14.5
      color: "$ink"
      bold: true
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        "Unbilled USD" across three reports
  - elementId: f2-row1-label
    elementType: text
    bounds: [512, 186, 250, 16]
    content:
      fontSize: 11.5
      color: "$ink"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        Reports A & B — certified metric
  - elementId: f2-row1-value
    elementType: text
    bounds: [762, 186, 134, 16]
    content:
      fontSize: 11.5
      color: "$ink"
      bold: true
      wrap: false
      align: [right, middle]
      text: |
        $6,049,649.77
  - elementId: f2-rule1
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [512, 208, 384, 1]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$line"}
  - elementId: f2-row2-label
    elementType: text
    bounds: [512, 214, 250, 16]
    content:
      fontSize: 11.5
      color: "$ink"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        Report C — hand-written SQL
  - elementId: f2-row2-value
    elementType: text
    bounds: [762, 214, 134, 16]
    content:
      fontSize: 11.5
      color: "$sl"
      bold: true
      wrap: false
      align: [right, middle]
      text: |
        $7,393,499.19
  - elementId: f2-rule2
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [512, 236, 384, 1]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$line"}
  - elementId: f2-gap
    elementType: text
    bounds: [512, 244, 384, 16]
    content:
      fontSize: 11.5
      color: "$ink"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        <p>The gap: <strong><span style="color:$sl">$1,343,849.42 — a 22% larger number</span></strong></p>
  - elementId: f2-note
    elementType: text
    bounds: [512, 272, 384, 60]
    content:
      fontSize: 10.5
      color: "$muted"
      italic: true
      lineHeight: 1.35
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>All three reports read the same tables. Report C re-wrote the formula by hand and counted a different set of delivered-but-uninvoiced tickets.</p>
  - elementId: f2-verdict
    elementType: text
    bounds: [512, 366, 384, 16]
    content:
      fontSize: 11.5
      color: "$ink"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        <p>Root cause: <strong><span style="color:$sl">logic</span></strong> — the formula lives in many places</p>

  # ---------- takeaway ----------
  - elementId: takeaway-rule
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [64, 424, 832, 1]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$line"}
  - elementId: takeaway
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 442, 832, 44]
    content:
      fontSize: 13.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.45
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>Two different root causes need two different tools: an <strong><span style="color:$ont">ontology</span></strong> governs <strong>meaning</strong>, a <strong><span style="color:$sl">semantic layer</span></strong> governs <strong>logic</strong>. The next two slides take them one at a time.</p>

  # ---------- footer ----------
  - elementId: footer-left
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 514, 560, 14]
    content:
      style: "$caption"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        Both failure modes documented in the EPM demo — party roles (o2c-meaning.ttl) and the Report A/B/C comparison
  - elementId: footer-right
    elementType: text
    bounds: [830, 514, 66, 14]
    content:
      style: "$caption"
      wrap: false
      align: [right, middle]
      text: |
        01 / 05
